From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: gate MCU timeout recovery on initialization

A patch-semaphore timeout during probe can queue reset_work before the
PHY scan workers have been initialized. The full recovery path then
tries to cancel the uninitialized scan work instead of allowing probe to
fail normally.

Require completed hardware initialization before starting recovery after
an MCU timeout. Serialize this check and enqueue with stop_recovery so
teardown cannot cancel recovery and then receive a new timeout work item.
Keep the timeout error and normal runtime recovery behavior unchanged.

Fixes: 07ae843cd42d ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: reset device after MCU message timeout")
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -463,15 +463,20 @@ mt7996_mcu_parse_response(struct mt76_de
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	if (!skb) {
+		unsigned long flags;
+
 		dev_err(mdev->dev, "Message %08x (seq %d) timeout\n",
 			cmd, seq);
 
-		if (!test_and_set_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state)) {
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->recovery_lock, flags);
+		if (!READ_ONCE(dev->removing) && dev->recovery.hw_init_done &&
+		    !test_and_set_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state)) {
 			dev->recovery.restart = true;
 			wake_up(&dev->mt76.mcu.wait);
 			queue_work(dev->mt76.wq, &dev->reset_work);
 			wake_up(&dev->reset_wait);
 		}
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->recovery_lock, flags);
 
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 	}
